arious practices and now clearly criminal actions. In fact, the space my pe=
rsonal property was moved into is NOT a locker. It is a closet with a singl=
e lock. A locker

Thank you, David.

As I have stated before, this landlord has engaged in nefarious practices a=
nd now clearly criminal actions. In fact, the space my personal property wa=
s moved into is NOT a locker. It is a closet with a single lock. A locker s=
hould be defined as a small lockable closet or compartment, typically as on=
e of a number placed together and the tenants belongings are ALWAYS protect=
ed by two locks - that of the locker itself and that of the storage facilit=
y. The landlord has attempted to rename the space being used, moved and pot=
entially damaged my property without my permission, which I expressly forba=
de, and the result is less security than I had before.

The measurements of the closet, which does not meet the requirements of den=
otation of meaning for 'locker' I will get later.

Please give me information on what forms I require for the filing of the cl=
aim.

Thank you,
Evan Rosner


On Thu, Feb 22, 2024 at 1:47=E2=80=AFPM Maclean, David <David.Maclean@gov.m=
b.ca<mailto:David.Maclean@gov.mb.ca>> wrote:
Hi Evan

Thank you for your patience.  I have received an email back from the landlo=
rd to advise that your belongings have been moved and the laundry has been =
disconnected.  Although the Branch is firm in its stance that the services =
must remain accessible (in its current state) until the permanent withdrawa=
l date, the Branch cannot do more than tell the landlord this.

The consequence of this though is that the withdrawal date will change.  I =
will be formulating an amount for the rent reduction for the withdrawal of =
the storage and laundry.

I have your current measurements of the unit as 90cm by 60 cm by 60cm.  Do =
you know what the provided locker space is?

Also for laundry; can you let me know where you now have to go for laundry =
services and how often you would have to go.  I also will be doing the same=
 but welcome your input as well.

Filing a claim.  You have every right, the landlord is also aware, that you=
 can file a claim with the Branch for financial loss.  This could be, but n=
ot restricted to=E2=80=A6. Any loss of personal items in the storage locker=
, laundry services, locker space.  A hearing would take place and a hearing=
 officer would make a ruling based on the evidence provided.

Please let me know if you have any questions, thank you Evan



